From 805a7f98366fe7a0e5c1b65f21cefb97e88adf54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexis Arnaudon <alexis.arnaudon@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:41:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Build libleidenalg in Release mode on Linux/macOS

build_libleidenalg.sh configured libleidenalg without CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE.
With single-config generators (Makefiles, used on Linux and macOS),
'cmake --build . --config Release' has no effect, so the library was
compiled without any optimisation flag (-O0): the shipped
liblibleidenalg.so exports out-of-line std::vector::operator[] and ~900
other STL helpers. build_igraph.sh already passes
-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release; do the same for libleidenalg.

Measured on a 20k-node CPM problem (one optimise_partition call): 2.2-2.6 s
with the shipped wheel vs 0.5-0.55 s with an optimised build, identical
memberships. Windows builds (multi-config generator) are not affected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 scripts/build_libleidenalg.sh | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/scripts/build_libleidenalg.sh b/scripts/build_libleidenalg.sh
index eacb545..41fa777 100755
--- a/scripts/build_libleidenalg.sh
+++ b/scripts/build_libleidenalg.sh
@@ -40,6 +40,7 @@ echo "Configure libleidenalg build"
 cmake ${ROOT_DIR}/build-deps/src/libleidenalg \
     -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=${ROOT_DIR}/build-deps/install/ \
     -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON \
+    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
     -Digraph_ROOT=${ROOT_DIR}/build-deps/install/lib/cmake/igraph/ \
     ${EXTRA_CMAKE_ARGS}
 
